To modify a specific section in a LaTeX document, you can use the `titlesec` package. This package allows you to customize the formatting of section titles, including the font size and style. Here's an example of how you can modify a section title to be italicized:
```
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{titlesec}
% Define a new section format with italicized title
\titleformat{\section}{\itshape\large}{\thesection}{1em}{}
\begin{document}
\section{Introduction}
This is the introduction section.
\section{Background}
This is the background section.
\end{document}
```
In this example, we first load the `titlesec` package. Then, we define a new section format using the `\titleformat` command. The first argument specifies the section level we want to modify (`\section`), the second argument specifies the font size and style we want to use (`\itshape\large` for italicized text with a larger font size), the third argument specifies the format of the section number (`\thesection`), the fourth argument specifies the distance between the section number and the title (1em), and the fifth argument is left empty to indicate that we don't want any additional formatting.
Finally, we use the modified `\section` command in our document, and the section titles will appear in italicized text with a larger font size.

