That is a great set of criteria for evaluating the reliability of AI models, and here is the Java code to calculate the overall reliability score based on these attributes:
```
import org.json.*;
public class AIEvaluation {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double accuracy = 0.8;
        double interpretability = 0.7;
        double scalability = 0.9;
        double robustness = 0.6;
        double computationalEfficiency = 0.8;
        double totalWeight = 0.0;
        double totalScore = 0.0;
        JSONObject criteria = new JSONObject("{\"Accuracy\":{\"weight\":0.3,\"description\":\"How accurately the model can predict the outcome\"},\"Interpretability\":{\"weight\":0.2,\"description\":\"How easy it is to understand and interpret the model\"},\"Scalability\":{\"weight\":0.2,\"description\":\"How well the model scales with increasing amounts of data\"},\"Robustness\":{\"weight\":0.15,\"description\":\"How well the model performs under various conditions and inputs\"},\"Computational Efficiency\":{\"weight\":0.15,\"description\":\"How fast the model can make predictions\"}}");
        for (String key : criteria.keySet()) {
            double weight = criteria.getJSONObject(key).getDouble("weight");
            totalWeight += weight;
            double score = 0.0;
            switch (key) {
                case "Accuracy":
                    score = accuracy;
                    break;
                case "Interpretability":
                    score = interpretability;
                    break;
                case "Scalability":
                    score = scalability;
                    break;
                case "Robustness":
                    score = robustness;
                    break;
                case "Computational Efficiency":
                    score = computationalEfficiency;
                    break;
            }
            totalScore += weight * score;
        }
        double overallScore = totalScore / totalWeight;
        System.out.println("Overall reliability score: " + overallScore);
    }
}
```
You can replace the values of accuracy, interpretability, scalability, robustness, and computationalEfficiency with the actual scores of the AI model you want to evaluate. The code will then calculate the overall reliability score based on the weights and descriptions of the criteria specified in the JSON data.

