    } yield List(a, b, c, d, e, f)
    if (solutions.nonEmpty) {
      println("Solutions found:")
      solutions.foreach(println)
    } else {
      println("No solutions found.")
    }
  }
}
```
This code uses a nested `for` loop to generate all possible permutations of the six numbers, and then checks whether each permutation can be combined with the four basic arithmetic operations to obtain the target value of 120. The `yield` keyword creates a list of solutions that satisfy the condition, and the `if` statement filters out solutions that don't.
Note that this code uses brute force to solve the puzzle, which means that it may take some time to run if there are many possible combinations of the six numbers. However, it should work correctly and find all solutions that exist.

