This code uses URLSession to download the PDF of the research paper and then uses a summarize function to extract a summary of 5 sentences from the paper data. You'll need to define the summarize function yourself or use a third-party library.

output:
Here's an example of how you could define the summarize function in Swift:
```
func summarize(_ paperData: Data, numSentences: Int) -> String {
    // Convert the paper data to a string
    guard let paperString = String(data: paperData, encoding: .utf8) else {
        return "Error: could not convert paper data to string"
    }

    // Split the paper into sentences
    let sentenceEnders = [".", "?", "!"]
    var sentences = paperString.components(separatedBy: CharacterSet(charactersIn: sentenceEnders).inverted)
    sentences = sentences.filter { !$0.isEmpty }

    // Calculate the score of each sentence based on the number of times it appears in the paper
    var scores = [Int](repeating: 0, count: sentences.count)
    for (i, sentence) in sentences.enumerated() {
        scores[i] = paperString.components(separatedBy: sentence).count - 1
    }

    // Sort the sentences by score and return the top numSentences
    let sortedSentences = sentences.enumerated().sorted { scores[$0.offset] > scores[$1.offset] }.map { $0.element }
    let summarySentences = Array(sortedSentences.prefix(numSentences))
    return summarySentences.joined(separator: " ")
}
```
You can then call this function in the URLSession completion handler like this:
```
let paper = "A Study on the Effect of Text Messaging on Student Performance"
let url = URL(string: "https://example.com/research_papers/\(paper).pdf")
let task = URLSession.shared.downloadTask(with: url!) { localURL, urlResponse, error in
  if let localURL = localURL {
    do {
      let paperData = try Data(contentsOf: localURL)
      let summary = summarize(paperData, numSentences: 5)
      print(summary)
    } catch {
      print("Error: \(error)")
    }
  }
}
task.resume()
```
This will download the PDF of the research paper and print a summary of the paper in 5 sentences.

